        "descriptionModule": {
          "briefSummary": "Antimicrobial resistance AMR is an emerging global threat to human health, and intensive care units (ICUs) are a 'hot spot' for the emergence and diffusion of multidrug-resistant (MDR) bacteria. ICU-acquired colonization and infection with MDR bacteria (ICU-MDR-col and ICU-MDR-inf, respectively) have been associated with higher ICU length-of-stay, duration of invasive mechanical ventilation and mortality. Immunocompromised patients account for an increasing prop

yond. Thus, we are planning to carry out the TANGERINE study, an observational prospective multicenter study in Europe, to confirm the findings of CIMDREA and provide a better understanding of the effect of isolation measures and contact precautions on the epidemiology of AMR in ICUs."
        },
